{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00633",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 10.35,
      "duration_seconds": 9.36,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I'm sorry to bother you again, I just don't like the look of my wound."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.39,
      "end_seconds": 19.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "You're not bothering me, that's why we're here. Which wound is this? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.69,
      "end_seconds": 29.33,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "The one from my hernia operation. I had it done two weeks ago, on the left side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.37,
      "end_seconds": 36.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "And what's wrong with it? What are you noticing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.66,
      "end_seconds": 49.43,
      "duration_seconds": 11.77,
      "text": "The skin round it has gone red, and it's warm. It was fine last week and then, um, over the weekend it changed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.75,
      "end_seconds": 55.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Any fever or shivering with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.45,
      "end_seconds": 62.54,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "No, no fever. I've felt a bit tired, but I've no temperature."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.4,
      "end_seconds": 75.94,
      "duration_seconds": 10.54,
      "text": "Good. I'll look in a moment, but first, let's go through your medicines, because I know there's a few."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.79,
      "end_seconds": 92.58,
      "duration_seconds": 15.79,
      "text": "Right. The antibiotic they gave me, flucloxacillin, maybe 500 mg, four times a day, I think? I'd have to check the box. Then paracetamol, 1 gram, when I need it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.19,
      "end_seconds": 104.46,
      "duration_seconds": 9.27,
      "text": "That's maybe 500 mg of the flucloxacillin, we'll check the box, thank you. What else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.07,
      "end_seconds": 117.35,
      "duration_seconds": 10.28,
      "text": "Ramipril, 2.5 mg once a day. Simvastatin, 20 mg at night. And my metformin, 500 mg twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.29,
      "end_seconds": 124.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "Good, that matches what I've got. And your background conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.88,
      "end_seconds": 133.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "Type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, and high cholesterol. All the usual suspects."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.99,
      "end_seconds": 137.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "And do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.57,
      "end_seconds": 145.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "I gave up two years ago after the diagnosis. Never going back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.62,
      "end_seconds": 152.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "Well done. Let me check your temperature and pulse. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.52,
      "end_seconds": 155.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.26,
      "end_seconds": 172.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Temperature 37.2, pulse 84."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.04,
      "end_seconds": 177.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Is that normal? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.93,
      "end_seconds": 188.6,
      "duration_seconds": 8.67,
      "text": "Just a touch warm, but no fever. Let's see this wound. Lie back for me. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.63,
      "end_seconds": 194.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "It's feeling tight when I move. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.57,
      "end_seconds": 222.9,
      "duration_seconds": 11.33,
      "text": "The skin around the wound is red and warm for about three centimetres, with no pus, and the stitches look intact."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.75,
      "end_seconds": 226.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Is it infected? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.33,
      "end_seconds": 237.37,
      "duration_seconds": 10.04,
      "text": "There's a bit of inflammation, so I'd like to take a swab from it, to see if any germs are growing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.72,
      "end_seconds": 242.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Does it hurt? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.53,
      "end_seconds": 255.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Hardly at all, it's a cotton bud. Done."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.68,
      "end_seconds": 265.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "Phew. And what about my antibiotic? Should I stay on it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.11,
      "end_seconds": 277.63,
      "duration_seconds": 10.52,
      "text": "Yes, finish the course as prescribed, and I'll check the swab before changing anything. Keep the wound clean and dry."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.72,
      "end_seconds": 283.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "I've been covering it with a plaster. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.17,
      "end_seconds": 295.44,
      "duration_seconds": 9.27,
      "text": "Leave it uncovered at home if you can, and change the plaster if it gets damp. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.47,
      "end_seconds": 302.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. And if it gets worse? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.72,
      "end_seconds": 317.61,
      "duration_seconds": 12.89,
      "text": "If the redness spreads, or you get a temperature or a lot of pain, come back to me straight away or go to the urgent care centre."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.46,
      "end_seconds": 322.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "I will. Thank you, doctor. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.66,
      "end_seconds": 328.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Take care, Mr Fisher. ~"
    }
  ]
}
